  "_title": "Resonance-Avoiding Beam — Disconnected Frequency Bands",
  "_purpose": "Find beam-dimension solution boxes that satisfy static stress and deflection limits while placing the first bending natural frequency outside the 60 Hz to 120 Hz excitation band.",
  "_fidelity": "Euler-Bernoulli analytical cantilever benchmark with E = 210 GPa, density = 7850 kg/m^3, and a 200 N tip proof load. The saved equations include 1e-12 numerical offsets in the second moment of area and cross-section area. Thick-beam effects, joints, damping, material scatter, and full modal FEA require downstream verification.",
  "_visual_target": "Inspect disjoint solution boxes separating low-frequency sub-resonance and high-frequency supra-resonance regimes.",
  "_engineering_decision": "Select rectangular beam height, width, and cantilever span that satisfy sigma <= 250 MPa, delta <= 10 mm, and f1 <= 60 Hz or f1 >= 120 Hz. The graph has no mass output or optimization objective; use it to explore feasible regions.",
  "_baseline": "At h = 45.0 mm, b = 25.0 mm, and L = 0.8 m, the saved equations give f1 = 58.740894 Hz, sigma = 18.962863 MPa, delta = 0.856172 mm, and signed resonance constraint f_n = -1.259106 Hz. This point is feasible and lies 2.10% below the 60 Hz band edge. The independently calculated solid beam mass is 7.065 kg; mass is not a graph output.",
  "_design_variables": [
    "Beam height h: 5.0 to 50.0 mm",
    "Beam width b: 10.0 to 100.0 mm",
    "Beam span length L: 0.3 to 1.0 m"
  ],
  "_load_cases": [
    "A 200 N static tip proof load for stress and deflection under clamped-free cantilever boundary conditions.",
    "First bending natural-frequency exclusion from the open interval (60 Hz, 120 Hz). The analytical model does not calculate a forced harmonic response."
  ],
  "_requirements": [
    {
      "name": "Resonance Avoidance Margin",
      "requirement": "The graph output f_n = min(f1 - 60 Hz, 120 Hz - f1) must be <= 0 Hz. Thus f1 <= 60 Hz or f1 >= 120 Hz is feasible; no extra clearance percentage is imposed. f_n is a signed exclusion constraint, not the natural frequency."
    },
    {
      "name": "Max Bending Stress",
      "requirement": "Static peak bending stress sigma must be between 0 Pa and 250000000 Pa under the 200 N tip proof load."
    },
    {
      "name": "Tip Deflection",
      "requirement": "Static tip deflection delta must be between 0 m and 0.01 m under the 200 N tip proof load."
    }
  ],
  "_deliverables": [
    "Multimodal feasible solution boxes isolating low-frequency and high-frequency design branches",
    "Static stress, tip-deflection, and signed frequency-exclusion response maps",
    "Recommended candidate beam geometry and verification modal parameters"
  ],
  "_workflow": [
    "Discover the feasible regions above and below the forbidden frequency band.",
    "Retain separate multimodal boxes rather than bridging the resonance gap.",
    "Compare the feasible branches using interval widths and verified static responses. Add an explicit mass output and objective if mass optimization is required."
  ],
  "_acceptance_criteria": [
    "Fresh validation samples satisfy sigma <= 250 MPa, delta <= 10 mm, and f_n <= 0 Hz.",
    "Retain separate boxes across the forbidden frequency interval. Finite sampling does not prove that every point in a box is feasible.",
    "Add explicit frequency clearance or material-uncertainty inputs if they are required; the saved graph does not impose them.",
    "Selected corners are checked with a modal finite-element model."
  ],
